    "result_text": "All 256 tests pass, including the new `AcceptanceTest`. The change is complete and green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `customerCode` assignment for owners, formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`.\n\n**How it works:** when an owner is created via `POST /api/owners`, the controller computes `LAST3` as the upper-cased first three letters of `lastName` and `NNNN` as a global 4-digit zero-padded sequence equal to one more than the current owner count, then persists and returns it (e.g. `SMI-0007`).\n\n**Files changed:**\n\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `customerCode` field (`@Column(name = \"customer_code\")`) with getter/setter.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 in `addOwner`, set `owner.setCustomerCode(nextCustomerCode(owner.getLastName()))` before saving; added the `nextCustomerCode` helper that builds `String.format(\"%s-%04d\", last3, findAllOwners().size() + 1)`. It's assigned only on create (not on update), so the code is immutable once set.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `customerCode` property to the `Owner` schema; the generated `OwnerDto` picks it up and MapStruct auto-maps it (same field name on entity and DTO), so it serializes on `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n- **Schema SQL** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added a `customer_code` column to the `owners` table. Tests run on hsqldb.\n\nNotes: the LAST3 computation safely handles last names shorter than three characters (`substring(0, min(3, len))`). The sequence is derived from the live owner count at creation time, which gives the required global +1 progression the acceptance test asserts.",
